1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Listen to me carefully, everyone. During this mission, I won't tolerate any failures. Follow my orders to the letter and don't fool around. This mission will probably be the most dangerous you will ever have. Many of you will die.

2
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Remember, everyone here is family. That means those who fall in battle are our brothers and sisters. But they won't die in vain. Their sacrifices will ensure our success. Let me be clear. Our goal isn't to come back alive. It is to be victorious no matter what. Do you understand?

3
00:02:02,998 --> 00:02:30,118
Shinoa, how much longer?

4
00:02:30,118 --> 00:02:32,438
We've got about 20 minutes.

5
00:02:32,998 --> 00:02:39,018
Everyone, fall in line.

6
00:02:39,018 --> 00:02:46,418
I want to go over our plan of attack again.

7
00:02:46,418 --> 00:02:48,938
We began at 1400 hours.

8
00:02:48,938 --> 00:02:51,918
Our gathered troops will move in teams, attacking in unison.

9
00:02:51,918 --> 00:02:56,378
If all goes as planned, eight targets will be executed, leaving two nobles alive.

10
00:02:56,378 --> 00:03:01,318
Our target's a strong one, Lukul Wesker, the 15th progenitor.

11
00:03:01,318 --> 00:03:04,078
We plan to engage him here.

12
00:03:04,078 --> 00:03:08,338
If we're unable to take him by surprise, our priority is to cut off his retreat and prevent

13
00:03:08,338 --> 00:03:10,378
him from joining the other nobles.

14
00:03:10,378 --> 00:03:14,138
Once our target is dead, we'll hold off any remaining vampires until the Lieutenant Colonel

15
00:03:14,138 --> 00:03:16,998
supplies us with new orders.

16
00:03:16,998 --> 00:03:20,878
In this case scenario, all the targets are killed simultaneously, and we don't have a problem

17
00:03:20,878 --> 00:03:24,018
regrouping and killing the remaining two nobles in Nagoya.

18
00:03:24,018 --> 00:03:27,838
If the targets aren't destroyed and the nobles join forces, there's no way we'll be able

19
00:03:27,838 --> 00:03:30,038
to beat them.

20
00:03:30,038 --> 00:03:35,498
All of our targets are located fairly close to one another, but since our assembled forces

21
00:03:35,498 --> 00:03:39,018
have been split into small groups, it should keep the targets busy.

22
00:03:39,018 --> 00:03:40,738
Our team's one of the smallest.

23
00:03:40,738 --> 00:03:43,658
That means there must be high expectations for us.

24
00:03:43,658 --> 00:03:47,978
Even though there aren't as many troops in our squad, failure is not an option.

25
00:03:47,978 --> 00:03:51,978
If you make a mistake, it'll affect the lives of all 100 of your comrades.

26
00:03:51,978 --> 00:03:52,978
You have to remember that.

27
00:03:52,978 --> 00:03:53,978
We will.

28
00:03:53,978 --> 00:03:58,598
Ah, right, so basically all we gotta do is kill this Lululala guy, right?

29
00:03:58,598 --> 00:03:59,598
No sweat.

30
00:03:59,598 --> 00:04:00,598
Come on, man.

31
00:04:00,598 --> 00:04:03,258
Fooling around will get us killed.

32
00:04:03,258 --> 00:04:04,878
This is behind enemy lines.

33
00:04:04,878 --> 00:04:06,878
Have you forgotten what the Lieutenant Colonel said?

34
00:04:06,878 --> 00:04:07,878
Huh?

35
00:04:07,878 --> 00:04:10,358
I'm just saying that it's not gonna be that hard.

36
00:04:10,358 --> 00:04:11,578
Show some respect.

37
00:04:11,578 --> 00:04:12,578
This kid.

38
00:04:12,578 --> 00:04:13,578
He isn't serious.

39
00:04:13,578 --> 00:04:16,358
Sergeant Narami, can't we be reassigned?

40
00:04:16,358 --> 00:04:19,038
There's no way I can trust these kids to have my back.

41
00:04:19,038 --> 00:04:21,118
Whoa, calm down, Rika.

42
00:04:21,118 --> 00:04:22,918
We have to work alongside them.

43
00:04:22,918 --> 00:04:25,858
We don't really have time to switch out.

44
00:04:25,858 --> 00:04:28,078
This kind of unrest isn't good.

45
00:04:28,078 --> 00:04:29,858
They hate us.

46
00:04:29,858 --> 00:04:31,858
Go apologize.

47
00:04:31,858 --> 00:04:35,718
Um, I apologize, Sergeant Narami.

48
00:04:35,718 --> 00:04:38,718
I'll make sure my squad is ready to follow order.

49
00:04:38,718 --> 00:04:41,038
I don't need anyone to apologize.

50
00:04:41,038 --> 00:04:43,518
Just remember, we need to be on our toes.

51
00:04:43,518 --> 00:04:47,198
If one person drags us down, then we're all as good as dead.

52
00:04:47,198 --> 00:04:50,798
I don't want to lose a comrade because of a single screw-up.

53
00:04:50,798 --> 00:04:53,738
What is it?

54
00:04:53,738 --> 00:04:55,238
Do you not agree with what I said?

55
00:04:55,238 --> 00:04:55,958
No.

56
00:04:55,958 --> 00:04:56,958
I mean, yes.

57
00:04:56,958 --> 00:04:59,898
What I'm saying is that I feel the same way.

58
00:04:59,898 --> 00:05:01,898
I don't want to lose any comrades either.

59
00:05:01,898 --> 00:05:02,898
I don't need excuses.

60
00:05:02,898 --> 00:05:03,898
I need you to act-

61
00:05:03,898 --> 00:05:04,898
Listen!

62
00:05:04,898 --> 00:05:11,898
Our squads, we're in this together, so I'll make sure that none of us get hurt.

63
00:05:11,898 --> 00:05:17,838
Then the least you can do is remember our target's name.

64
00:05:17,838 --> 00:05:20,838
There's more to being a good soldier than the ability to swing a sword.

65
00:05:20,838 --> 00:05:24,838
There's no point in remembering the name of someone you're just going to kill.

66
00:05:24,838 --> 00:05:30,778
But, I do remember the names of the people I'm going to protect.

67
00:05:30,778 --> 00:05:32,778
Got it?

68
00:05:32,778 --> 00:05:47,838
Shinoa, Kimizuki, Mitsuba, Yoichi, Makoto Narumi, Yayoi Endo, Rika Inoue, Taro Kageyama, Shusaku Iwasuki.

69
00:05:47,838 --> 00:05:50,838
I won't let my comrades get killed.

70
00:05:50,838 --> 00:05:54,838
We'll show Gorin we can be victorious without losing a single teammate.

71
00:05:54,838 --> 00:05:59,838
